# Store and check out every file byte-for-byte, with no line-ending
# translation.  This matters here for three reasons:
#
#   * org-doc/ holds the original distribution's documentation -- leave those
#     bytes exactly as distributed;
#   * test/*.sh and src/makefile must keep LF endings to work under POSIX
#     shells and make, including from WSL on a Windows checkout;
#   * if you drop the original sample/ directory in here to run the regression
#     suite, its *.mml must stay byte-identical or the recorded SHA-256
#     baseline will not match.
#
# Without this, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite all of the
# above to CRLF.
* -text

# Explicitly binary, so Git never tries to diff or merge them as text.
*.mid binary
